{"id":2346,"age":8,"sex":"M","race":"Non-Hispanic White","insurance":"Commercial insurance (Blue Cross Blue Shield)","profile":{"sex":"M","allergies":["No known drug allergies"],"insurance":"Commercial insurance (Blue Cross Blue Shield)","occupation":"Elementary school student (3rd grade)","alcohol_use":"Never","family_history":["Type 1 diabetes mellitus in maternal uncle","Autoimmune hypothyroidism in paternal grandmother","Celiac disease in second cousin (maternal)"],"race_ethnicity":"Non-Hispanic White","smoking_status":"Never smoker","home_medications":[],"surgical_history":[],"chronic_conditions":[],"age_at_first_encounter":8},"comorbidities_listed":["Upper respiratory tract infection","Dehydration","Type 1 diabetes mellitus"],"primary":{"did":527,"code":"E10.10","name":"Diabetic ketoacidosis"},"filing":{"chapter":4,"block":"E08-E13","block_desc":"Diabetes mellitus (E08-E13)"},"encounters":[{"id":10044,"date":"2020-01-15","type":"inpatient","dept":"Pediatrics","attending":"Dr. Sarah Chen","cc":"Progressively worsening fatigue, vomiting, and deep breathing","order":0,"method":"template","question_ids":[4309],"sections":[{"sid":35977,"type":"chief_complaint","lines":["Progressively worsening fatigue, vomiting, and deep breathing"]},{"sid":35978,"type":"hpi","lines":["His parents report that he recently recovered from a mild febrile illness that included nasal congestion and sore throat.","Over the past four days, he has been excessively thirsty and urinating much more frequently than usual, including at night.","He has also appeared more tired and irritable and has complained of occasional abdominal discomfort.","This morning, he was found lying on the bathroom floor breathing rapidly, and his parents noticed a fruity odor on his breath.","They also say he has seemed a bit confused and \"not himself.\""]},{"sid":35979,"type":"pmh","lines":["Previously healthy"]},{"sid":35980,"type":"allergies","lines":["No known drug allergies"]},{"sid":35981,"type":"family_history","lines":["- Type 1 diabetes mellitus in maternal uncle","- Autoimmune hypothyroidism in paternal grandmother","- Celiac disease in second cousin (maternal)"]},{"sid":35982,"type":"social_history","lines":["Smoking: Never smoker. Alcohol: Never. Occupation: Elementary school student (3rd grade)."]},{"sid":35983,"type":"vitals","lines":["Tachycardic, and hypotensive. His respiratory rate is 32/min"]},{"sid":35984,"type":"physical_exam","lines":["On physical examination, the boy is drowsy.","His skin is dry, mucous membranes are parched, and capillary refill is delayed.","His breathing is deep and labored.","He is oriented only to person and appears ill."]},{"sid":35985,"type":"labs","lines":["A urine dipstick test is positive for both ketones and glucose.","Labs reveal hyperglycemia, metabolic acidosis with a high anion gap, and signs of volume depletion.","Serum electrolytes are abnormal but consistent with the suspected diagnosis.","Despite the hypotension, the child's glomerular filtration rate (GFR) is noted to be elevated on laboratory assessment."]}],"orders":[]},{"id":10046,"date":"2020-07-15","type":"ed","dept":"Emergency Medicine","attending":"Dr. Marcus Johnson","cc":"Vomiting, abdominal pain, and rapid breathing for the past day","order":1,"method":"hybrid","question_ids":[4304],"sections":[{"sid":35986,"type":"chief_complaint","lines":["Vomiting, abdominal pain, and rapid breathing for the past day"]},{"sid":35987,"type":"hpi","lines":["The patient returns to the emergency department six months after his prior admission for diabetic ketoacidosis, now presenting with similar complaints.","One week ago, he had a low-grade fever, sore throat, and fatigue that resolved without treatment.","Over the past several days, his parents noticed that he was drinking water almost constantly and urinating frequently during both the day and night.","This morning, he appeared drowsy and complained of stomach pain before vomiting twice."]},{"sid":35988,"type":"pmh","lines":["Active Problem List:","- Diabetic ketoacidosis (diagnosed 2020-01-15)"]},{"sid":35989,"type":"allergies","lines":["No known drug allergies"]},{"sid":35990,"type":"family_history","lines":["- Type 1 diabetes mellitus in maternal uncle","- Autoimmune hypothyroidism in paternal grandmother","- Celiac disease in second cousin (maternal)"]},{"sid":35991,"type":"social_history","lines":["Smoking: Never smoker. Alcohol: Never. Occupation: Elementary school student (3rd grade)."]},{"sid":35992,"type":"vitals","lines":["His temperature is 37.6\u00b0C (99.7\u00b0F), blood pressure is 90/52 mm Hg, heart rate is 132/min, and respiratory rate is 34/min with deep, labored breaths."]},{"sid":35993,"type":"physical_exam","lines":["On arrival, he is lethargic and mildly confused.","Capillary refill is delayed and his mucous membranes are dry."]},{"sid":35994,"type":"labs","lines":["Laboratory studies reveal a serum glucose of 594 mg/dL, serum bicarbonate of 7 mEq/L, and an arterial pH of 7.03.","Serum ketones are elevated, and urine is positive for both glucose and ketones."]},{"sid":35995,"type":"other_studies","lines":["Further testing reveals the presence of anti\u2013glutamic acid decarboxylase 65 (GAD65) antibodies.","His C-peptide level is undetectable, and his hemoglobin A1c is 12.2%."]},{"sid":35996,"type":"assessment","lines":["Diabetic ketoacidosis"]},{"sid":35997,"type":"plan","lines":["After initiating IV fluids and insulin therapy, he is admitted to the pediatric intensive care unit.","The patient and his parents are counseled on long-term insulin therapy, continuous glucose monitoring, and sick-day management."]}],"orders":[]},{"id":10045,"date":"2021-01-15","type":"icu","dept":"Pediatric Critical Care","attending":"Dr. Priya Sharma","cc":"Increasing lethargy and reduced responsiveness","order":2,"method":"hybrid","question_ids":[4209],"sections":[{"sid":35998,"type":"chief_complaint","lines":["Increasing lethargy and reduced responsiveness"]},{"sid":35999,"type":"hpi","lines":["The patient is a 9-year-old male with a history of two prior diabetic ketoacidosis admissions in January and July 2020 who presents to the Pediatric Critical Care ICU with increasing lethargy and reduced responsiveness.","Over the past week, the child had a sore throat, mild fever, and fatigue, which resolved spontaneously a few days ago.","Since then, he has been urinating far more frequently than usual and often wakes at night to use the bathroom.","His father reports that he has been drinking water almost constantly and seems to have lost weight despite eating normally.","Earlier today, the boy became noticeably weak and confused, prompting his father to bring him in."]},{"sid":36000,"type":"pmh","lines":["Active Problem List:","- Diabetic ketoacidosis (diagnosed 2020-01-15)"]},{"sid":36001,"type":"medications","lines":["He is not on any medications"]},{"sid":36002,"type":"allergies","lines":["No known drug allergies"]},{"sid":36003,"type":"family_history","lines":["- Type 1 diabetes mellitus in maternal uncle","- Autoimmune hypothyroidism in paternal grandmother","- Celiac disease in second cousin (maternal)"]},{"sid":36004,"type":"social_history","lines":["Smoking: Never smoker. Alcohol: Never. Occupation: Elementary school student (3rd grade)."]},{"sid":36005,"type":"vitals","lines":["He is tachycardic and hypotensive but afebrile."]},{"sid":36006,"type":"physical_exam","lines":["On examination, he is drowsy, has dry mucous membranes, and is breathing rapidly and deeply.","His extremities are cool, and his capillary refill is delayed.","Breath odor is fruity.","Neurologically, he is slow to respond but follows commands."]},{"sid":36007,"type":"labs","lines":["A urine dipstick is positive for glucose and ketones.","Labs are sent and confirm the suspected diagnosis."]}],"orders":[]}],"problems":[{"did":527,"code":"E10.10","name":"Diabetic ketoacidosis","icd_desc":"Type 1 diabetes mellitus with ketoacidosis without coma","snomed":"420422005","sno